  exe_gui.pcpp - Build-kind compliance: a gui exe (Windows)

  @subsystem gui builds a Windows program with no console window (BNF.md
  sec 2); it shows a message box through the Win32 API it #includes.
  Built by the tester, never run: a person checks the window.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\exe_gui.pcpp -r
  CHECK: a message box "exe_gui" saying "a gui program" appears, and no
  console window; OK closes it and the program ends.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe exe_gui;
@subsystem gui;

#include <windows.h>

begin
  // A C++ statement in a body goes in a cppstart block (BNF.md sec 10)
  cppstart source
  MessageBoxW(nullptr, L"a gui program", L"exe_gui", MB_OK);
  cppend;
end.
